cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "EndoTarget Evidence: cross-study target prioritization in endometriosis using donor-level transcriptomics, host-controlled lesion modeling, and human genetics"
abstract: >-
  Public-data endometriosis target-evidence study spanning cross-sectional eutopic
  endometrium and host-controlled ectopic lesions. Combines donor-level pseudobulk
  modeling across four single-cell/single-nucleus cohorts (GSE266265, HECA E-MTAB-14039,
  GSE179640, GSE213216; 561,364 retained cells/nuclei) and three tissue microarray cohorts
  (GSE51981, GSE6364, and 408-array / 162-subject multi-lesion and host-peritoneum cohort
  GSE141549), controlled comparisons of differential expression, global STRING network
  propagation, dual-contrast host-tissue decontamination, and vascular/myeloid niche
  ligand-receptor integration, plus germline genetics from Open Targets and Rahmioglu et al.
  (2023) under pre-external SHA-256 freezes and Nextflow/Docker replay checks. Cross-sectional
  eutopic stromal fibroblasts yield zero cross-study targets (median bound < 1.5-1.8x),
  whereas host-controlled lesion modeling exposes 100% peritoneal host-background false
  positives in naive lesion DE, establishes significant cross-cohort lesion transfer and
  germline genetic enrichment, and prioritizes RUNX1 alongside contextual niche and GWAS
  candidates.
